# Exploratory-spike API caches (~140MB). Both spikes hit free, keyless, public
# endpoints -- NIH RePORTER + iCite for funding_spike, Overpass + Microsoft
# Global ML Building Footprints for osm_spike -- and each script carries a
# provenance footer with the exact refetch command. The osm_spike Overpass
# cache is content-addressed on the full query string, so a refetch repopulates
# it under identical names.
/artifacts_scripts/funding_spike/cache/
/artifacts_scripts/funding_spike/*.log
/artifacts_scripts/osm_spike/cache/

# The paper lives in its own nested git repo under /paper/. It is
# intentionally not tracked here; edit and commit it from within the
# paper repo itself. The explicit ignore line prevents an accidental
# `git add` from registering it as a stray gitlink.
/paper/

# Survey response data. Contains participant email addresses, IP addresses and
# geolocation, plus PureSpectrum panel re-identification keys. Purged from git
# history 2026-08-01; kept locally because the paper's Tables 4 and 8 are
# generated from it by artifacts_scripts/survey/verify_survey_alignment.py.
# Do not re-add.
artifacts_scripts/survey/Survey_finalresults.csv
artifacts_scripts/survey/Survey_+Textbook+Proposal+Evaluation_*.csv
# Generated by generate_survey.py from selected_books.csv. Purged from history
# 2026-08-01 because it embedded institutional branding; regenerate it rather
# than committing it.
artifacts_scripts/survey/survey.qsf

# Reconstructed publisher abstracts. OpenAlex ships abstracts as an inverted
# index rather than plain text precisely so it is not redistributing the
# abstract as a text; reconstructing one and committing it undoes that. Their
# CC0 grant covers the OpenAlex database, not third-party abstract copyright.
# 24 abstracts, 1416-2878 chars each.
#
# Kept locally so generate_survey.py still runs; regenerate from scratch with
#   uv run python artifacts_scripts/survey/select_survey_books.py
# Not even an abstract-free metadata variant is published: it would name specific
# real books as the "less-cited" arm, with percentiles, which is uncharitable to
# those authors for no reproducibility gain the paper does not already give.
artifacts_scripts/survey/selected_books.csv
artifacts_scripts/survey/survey.txt

# Emacs lock files. Four were committed by accident and purged from history
# 2026-08-02; they encode user@host.pid and are never wanted in a repo.
.#*

# Editor settings (VS Code), per machine rather than per project.
.vscode/
